{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is satisfied.** The implementation covers both obligations and the tests exercise the interesting cases. One minor marking point is noted at the end.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` defines `setup --path <crate-dir>` as an optional `PathBuf`. It passes the value to `setup::run`.\n- `src/setup.rs` `has_habeas_dev_dependency` is marked `{impl}`. It returns true when `[dev-dependencies]` already has a `habeas` entry.\n- `run` (marked `{impl}` for this requirement at line ~161) skips the dependency step when that function returns true. This gives the \"no existing Habeas dev dependency\" condition and the \"repeating setup must not add a duplicate\" rule.\n- When there is no existing dev dependency and `--path` is given, `run` calls `cargo add --dev habeas --manifest-path <Cargo.toml> --path <canonicalized crate-dir>`.\n- Canonicalizing means a relative `--path` is resolved from the invocation directory. A nonexistent directory fails before the manifest is changed.\n- A failing `cargo add` is reported as an error.\n- Without `--path`, `run` adds the dependency from the registry instead. The `setup` requirement covers that case, and `run` is also marked `{impl}` for `setup`.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/setup.rs`, all marked `{test}`)\n- `local_path_setup_adds_exactly_that_crate_once` uses a relative `--path` and checks three things:\n  - exactly one `habeas` entry exists across the dependency tables;\n  - that entry is in `dev-dependencies`;\n  - its path resolves to the requested crate.\n\n  It then repeats setup with an absolute path and checks that `Cargo.toml` is byte-identical.\n- `local_path_setup_keeps_an_existing_habeas_dev_dependency` starts with a pre-existing `habeas = \"0.1\"` dev dependency. After `--path` setup the manifest is unchanged, so there is no duplicate and no replacement.\n- `local_path_setup_rejects_a_missing_crate_directory` is the failure case. Setup exits non-zero, `Cargo.toml` is unchanged, and no `habeas` dependency is added.\n- `setup_is_repeatable` runs setup twice with `--path` and checks that a path dependency is present in `[dev-dependencies]`.\n- `habeas_dependencies` is a helper marked `{test}`.\n\n**Marking and extra behaviour**\n- I found no behaviour in the `{impl}` code that the requirement or another cited requirement leaves unspecified.\n- The `--path` argument declaration in `Command::Setup` is covered by the `clap` and `setup` markers rather than a direct `setup_local_path` marker. It is plain option plumbing, so I do not count it as a gap.",
